# Frontend environment variables. Vite exposes only VITE_-prefixed vars to the app.
#
# You do NOT need any of this for local development. Leave VITE_API_BASE_URL unset
# and the app calls the API with relative paths (/api/v1/...), which vite.config.js
# proxies to the backend on localhost:8000. Just run `docker compose up` and
# `npm run dev` and the two halves talk.
#
# Set it only when DEPLOYING. The Vite proxy is a dev-server feature and does not
# exist in a production build, so a frontend on Vercel/Netlify talking to a backend
# on Render needs the absolute origin here (set it in the host's dashboard, not in
# a committed file):
#
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-backend.onrender.com/api/v1
#
# To override locally anyway, copy this to frontend/.env.local (gitignored).
